@* Shared loading-skeleton component every screen renders during the static-prerender pass instead
   of fetching (RendererInfo.IsInteractive gating, issue #86) — built on Bootstrap's already-vendored
   placeholder/placeholder-glow utilities per #90's "What to build", not exact-layout-mimicking
   markup or bespoke per-screen CSS. §8 calls out "the design's placeholder counts" but no prototype
   file specifies one (#86's resolution), so Count defaults to a single card and callers repeat it
   as needed. *@
@for (var i = 0; i < Count; i++)
{
    <div class="card mb-3" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="card-body placeholder-glow">
            <h5 class="card-title"><span class="placeholder col-6"></span></h5>
            <p class="card-text">
                <span class="placeholder col-7"></span>
                <span class="placeholder col-4"></span>
                <span class="placeholder col-4"></span>
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
}

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public int Count { get; set; } = 1;
}
